      "writtenOn": "2014-08-23T20:18:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this is very very long story....\n\n\nFirst of all what is this: \n\n  HMAC keys are used to limit access to profiler. E.g. only person who knows HMAC can trigger profiling (even if it is enabled). \n\n\nWhy this was added: \n\n  Druing Atlanta cross-project session http://junodesignsummit.sched.org/event/54d25c4c4017ca09ee130821ac93f804#.U_jxCry1bq0 A lot of Operators said they want to have this ON on real production clouds and have some kind of \"profiling on demand\" without restarting whole cloud. As well the second criteria was to make it secure, e.g. only admin can trigger this stuff.\n\n\nWhy we have HMAC_KEYS and not only one\n\n  This was requirement from TripleO team. They said that security guys would like to change this HMAC_KEY periodically, from other side, if you change it directly (you\u0027ll get some some kind of downtime in ability to profile). Cause other project will use different HMAC_KEY from this. So to organize smooth change (without downtime) of HMAC you can specify any amount of them (and any will pass). \n\n  So algorithm to update HMAC key will be next: \n\n  INIT: \n  * Service1: HMAC_KEYS \u003d A \n  * Service2: HMAC_KEYS \u003d A\n\n   FIRST STEP: \n  * Service1: HMAC_KEYS \u003d A, B # restart all service 1\n  * Service2: HMAC_KEYS \u003d A\n\n  SECOND STEP:\n  * Service1: HMAC_KEYS \u003d A, B\n  * Service2: HMAC_KEYS \u003d A, B # restart all service2\n\n  THRID STEP:\n  * Service1: HMAC_KEYS \u003d B # restart all service 1\n  * Service2: HMAC_KEYS \u003d A, B \n\n  FINISH: \n  * Service1: HMAC_KEYS \u003d B \n  * Service2: HMAC_KEYS \u003d B # restart all service 2\n\n \n\nAbout keystone.conf  \u0026 HMAC_KEYS specification \n\n  This HMAC_KEY is used only in Middleware, so it won\u0027t be specified in keystone.conf. Also middleware doesn\u0027t know about oslo.config. So this is the simplest and cleanest way to pass it to middleware.",
      "parentUuid": "1abeadc6_824c2844",
      "revId": "1d7c78bbb0e370e83c141dcde0a5da704318c149",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
